    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch04-04: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.71";
    dc:description "Camouflage has direct, discriminating experimental measures and many reusable datasets. Coverage is insufficient for all animals exposed to visual predators, so the broad scope is only partially resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Measure visual contrast between prey and natural backgrounds, then relate contrast to detection, attack, survival and heritable colour variation. Lower detection and higher survival for background-matching phenotypes, together with selection on colour, support the claim.";
